id: pm-web-64ke
title: Resolve human-agent decisions in a shared inbox
description: "Collaborative web workflow over core Plan decisions with alternatives, evidence and audited SDK responses. Concurrent responses use revision checks; view-only users cannot apply; acknowledgments never count as code review or task completion. Typed SDK and CLI, compact TOON/JSON, remedies, docs, no-git and public tracker validation, browser screenshots."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-21T21:16:20.214Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-22T13:55:04.436Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Concurrent responses use revision checks; view-only users cannot apply; acknowledgment never counts as code review or task completion. Typed SDK and CLI, compact TOON/JSON, typed refusals with remedies, README and example, real public tracker validation and before/after screenshots."
comments[20]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T21:16:39.009Z",codex-agent,"Overlap checked against installed CLI 2026.10.21 and pinned SDK 2026.10.19: core plan decision stores decision text, rationale and evidence; no pending request workflow. Sibling pm-review owns typed review findings/verdicts and remote review completion. pm-jev owns model proposals. This feature adds a versioned web workflow within existing Plan decision logs, without another item type, review verdict, execution approval or completion model. Search inbox returned no existing package item. Tracker-reconciliation items are excluded. Plan: shared typed service, bounded CLI/HTTP, revision checks inside SDK cross-process lock, existing audited planDecision mutations, accessible comparison UI, real no-git/concurrency/refusal tests, public corpus read-only measurements, screenshots and CI npm/Bun release gates."
  "2026-10-21T21:25:34.442Z",codex-agent,"Implementation uses existing core planDecision mutations and a public SDK token-owned lock around revision check plus append. Independent processes sharing one non-git tracker: exactly one approval succeeded; the other received revision_conflict. Real HTTP owner/editor/viewer/stranger scenarios passed 2/2; view-only requests refused before mutation, and plan status/mode/steps stayed unchanged. Public main corpus validation: 172 items, 0 Plans, 2 Decision items, 0 pending requests; 85 JSON bytes, certified corpus plus inbox read 473 ms; 374 read-only source files retained identical aggregate SHA-256 43d589b8e5e7cd1ca0b51387518b56efb6aee7993d71540074ca76babe9595b4. Active workflow behavior uses separate real seeded fixtures because the public corpus has no Plans. Targeted service/command coverage: 99.49 percent lines, 88.96 branches, 100 functions before final native CLI additions. Full npm/Bun gates delegated to package CI per owner CPU constraint."
  "2026-10-21T21:30:55.366Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: temporarily removed only the editor-capability refusal and respondToDecision revision refusal, rebuilt server output, then ran node --test --test-name-pattern \"refusals reject|requests preserve|independent processes\" test/decision-inbox.test.ts. All 3 selected tests failed (0 passed), proving permission and revision assertions detect the reverted behavior. Restored both guards and rebuilt successfully. Cross-process race also uses canonical versus uppercase plan aliases to prove a shared lock identity. PM-linked targeted run passed 21/21 with no skips. Browser acceptance produced 5 local seeded screenshots and verified 1440/390 layouts, view-only disabled controls, unsent reasoning preservation after real SSE activity, acknowledgment pending, and approval without step completion. Isolated package health passed; default local health only had an unrelated globally installed extension version skew. Pins and reconciliation items remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-21T21:32:02.542Z",codex-agent,"Final restored targeted verification passed 21/21, zero failures or skips. Server/frontend typecheck, test compilation, lint, docstrings and zero-duplication gates passed at unchanged policy. Executable SDK example is included in package files. Source public-corpus measurements and local browser assertions are documented in docs/decision-inbox.md. Implementation is ready for PR validation; CI must supply full npm and Bun release:check evidence and screenshot artifact. Item intentionally remains in progress for orchestrator review; no merge, release or hosted changes."
  "2026-10-21T21:41:37.727Z",codex-agent,"First CI run 39679691912 failed only the two workflow action-policy regressions: both Node 22 and 26 suites reported 770/772 passed, 2 failed. The new screenshot upload action had an immutable official pin but was absent from the explicit action-name allowlist. Add only actions/upload-artifact to the existing approved actions supplier policy; retain all immutable-pin, release-comment and adversarial supplier checks. This is required screenshot evidence plumbing, not a threshold change. Re-run the workflow-policy tests locally, then the full CI release gates."
  "2026-10-21T21:43:26.365Z",codex-agent,"Added only actions/upload-artifact to the explicit workflow action-name allowlist. Official actions/upload-artifact v7.0.2 tag resolves to the already pinned cf430e030ddbb5b0abf93d22962f4752f3646cd9. No supplier owner, pin validation, release-version validation, adversarial assertion or coverage threshold changed. PM-linked restored feature tests passed 21/21 and workflow-policy tests passed 7/7; lint passed. First failed CI receipt is retained above. Ready to re-run the full npm/Bun CI gate and publish screenshot attachments."
  "2026-10-22T09:38:08.351Z",codex-agent,"PR 238 review round: all threads/comments fetched; PRRT_kwDOSZgR5c6vAu7Q is valid. Latest CodeRabbit body contains no Outside diff range findings. Pulled branch and merged origin/main. Separate loading/count/error status from interactive results and clear aria-busy after completion. Whole PR diff inspected for the same live-region defect; per-form response statuses already contain only short feedback. Browser regression covers loading, populated, SSE refresh, empty and error states. Initial npm ci hit inherited allow-scripts configuration; retry uses an isolated npm user config without changing pins or repository policy."
  "2026-10-22T09:42:05.136Z",codex-agent,"Dependency installation now passed with zero audit vulnerabilities using an isolated npm user config. npm run build and npm run build:test passed. Tracker health passed strict exit with only stale_in_progress_items advisory; no pending merge reconciliation was reported. Browser regression and behavioral revert verification are next, then complete npm and Bun release gates at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-22T09:44:31.192Z",codex-agent,"Browser acceptance passed on real local HTTP, PostgreSQL permissions and a seeded non-git tracker: 5 screenshots plus loading, populated, SSE-refreshed, empty, failed and recovered status-boundary assertions. No interactive results/forms are inside a live region; per-form response feedback remains separate. Now reverting only renderDecisionInbox to its prior implementation, keeping browser assertions and rebuilding frontend output for the failure proof."
  "2026-10-22T09:46:45.050Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof for PRRT_kwDOSZgR5c6vAu7Q: restored only the prior renderDecisionInbox function, retained browser assertions, ran npm run build:frontend then node scripts/with-test-db.ts node scripts/decision-inbox-browser.ts. Exit 1: AssertionError loading and count feedback need a separate live status (actual 0, expected 1). Restored fixed function and rebuilt frontend successfully. The fixed browser run had passed before the revert; PM-linked restored run follows."
  "2026-10-22T09:59:32.271Z",codex-agent,"Additional thread tool warnings checked: the header innerHTML contains static text plus a boolean edit-permission branch, so the generic unsanitized-input warnings do not identify an injection path. Request question, evidence, author, timestamp, plan id and alternative labels use escHtml; indexes and counts are server-derived numbers; loading/count/error feedback uses textContent. No additional instance of a live region wrapping interactive content was found in the complete PR diff. Restored PM-linked browser command passed 1/1, exit 0, after the behavioral revert failure. Changelog full/check and default strict health with isolated identity passed."
  "2026-10-22T10:09:04.075Z",codex-agent,"Local isolated-identity npm release:check passed typecheck, lint, zero duplication and 819 documented declarations, then hit the existing catalog-install-e2e built case 300-second timeout and a follow-on source-case failure. The suite reached at least 153 passed markers, including inbox HTTP/service/concurrency/native CLI tests, with those 2 catalog failures. Stopped the already-failed local run to avoid further shared-host load. This is incomplete local release evidence, not a pass. Per owner allowance, the pushed commit must pass complete npm and Bun release:check in CI at unchanged thresholds before the next PR starts. Browser acceptance separately passed restored PM-linked 1/1; revert proof and strict health/changelog checks passed."
  "2026-10-22T10:23:59.050Z",codex-agent,"CI 39761439056 on 988f0cd exposed a real main-merge integration defect: Node 22 passed 778/780 tests, with only two workflow-policy assertions failing and zero skipped/canceled/todo. Main added a graph screenshot-only uploader exception, while the feature branch previously globally approved actions/upload-artifact. Fix by removing global uploader approval and explicitly allowing only ci.yml and graph-scale-evidence.yml, retaining all SHA/release/owner checks. Add adversarial checks refusing unrelated and release workflows, prove a behavioral revert fails, then rerun the full npm/Bun CI gates. The catalog cases that timed out locally passed in CI."
  "2026-10-22T10:25:20.204Z",codex-agent,"Workflow integration regression passed 8/8, zero failures/skips. Behavioral revert: changed only assertWorkflowActionPins to restore the prior global uploader-approval behavior, leaving the new refusal cases intact. node --test --test-name-pattern \"pinned artifact uploader\" test/workflow-security.test.ts exited 1 with Missing expected exception for an unrelated/release workflow. Restored the scoped function. Only ci.yml and graph-scale-evidence.yml may use the pinned uploader; unrelated filenames remain refused. All immutable SHA, release, supplier, reusable-workflow and CodeQL checks remain intact. Restored PM-linked workflow verification follows."
  "2026-10-22T10:27:20.196Z",codex-agent,"Restored workflow policy passed through pm test --run --progress --only-index 2: 1/1 linked command, 8/8 tests, zero failures/skips. Scoped-upload behavioral revert failed 1 selected regression, 0 passed, 0 skipped; restoring the scoped function passed again. First CI catalog built/source cases passed in about 42/43 seconds, confirming the local 300-second timeout did not recur there. The first full gate remains failed on the workflow-policy integration; the corrected head requires fresh complete npm and Bun gates. No thresholds, action pins, dependency pins or workflow permissions changed."
  "2026-10-22T10:55:44.358Z",codex-agent,"Successful CI receipt on code head fd74fcd51327cf962713cb12b28220a1c1f7354b: run 39763568660, Node 26 job 119773409965 completed successfully. Both npm run release:check and bun run release:check passed at unchanged thresholds. Each passed 780/780 suite tests plus 2/2 capacity tests and 4/4 packed npm/Bun consumer scenarios; zero failures, skips, cancellations or todo. Coverage reconciled all 49 server source files: 92.97 percent statements/lines, 83.05 branches, 96.41 functions. Browser acceptance passed five synthetic screenshots and all new live-region states; artifact 12420815836. A separate packed acceptance also passed 4/4. Node 22 is still finishing its Bun gate at this receipt. Prior local catalog timeout passed in CI. This tracker receipt changes no code, pins, thresholds or workflow permissions; final pushed head checks will be verified before starting PR 237. CI: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/actions/runs/39763568660"
  "2026-10-22T13:44:08.580Z",codex-agent,"New review round: pulled the existing remote head and merged current main before edits. Reusing this item. Verify CLI dependency error exit codes, strict pagination coercion on HTTP and CLI, malformed stored envelopes, and response lock cleanup. Retain write validation and fail-closed integrity semantics; add behavioral regressions and record isolated revert proofs. Prior review gates remain historical evidence; this round will receive fresh full npm and Bun release gates."
  "2026-10-22T13:53:41.630Z",codex-agent,"Verified and fixed both current threads: PRRT_kwDOSZgR5c6vM-nA maps 503 to DEPENDENCY_FAILED (5), retaining USAGE (2), NOT_FOUND and CONFLICT; PRRT_kwDOSZgR5c6vM-nQ rejects blank, whitespace and repeated HTTP pagination values while keeping absent defaults. Whole-PR review found the same CLI pagination coercion and untyped complete-list failure; both now share the typed contract. Latest review body has no Outside diff range section, but both service nitpicks are valid: cleanup is best-effort and malformed stored envelopes now fail closed with invalid_record (503), naming the affected Plan. The latter follows the distinct-error alternative in the finding, retaining strict write validation and refusing ambiguous duplicate requests instead of silently dropping them."
  "2026-10-22T13:53:43.307Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs, with all new assertions retained and npm run build:server succeeding after each isolated revert: (1) runInboxCommand restored from the prior head: 0/2 pass; dependency exit actual 2 versus expected 5, and blank CLI offset accepted. Command: node scripts/with-test-db.ts node --test --test-name-pattern \"CLI inbox refusals|CLI inbox pagination\" test/decision-inbox.test.ts. (2) decisionRoute restored: 0/1 pass, offset= actual HTTP 200 versus expected 400. Command: node scripts/with-test-db.ts node --test --test-name-pattern \"HTTP inbox pagination\" test/decision-inbox-routes.test.ts. (3) project restored: 0/2 pass, malformed storage reported invalid_input/400 instead of invalid_record/503. Command: node scripts/with-test-db.ts node --test --test-name-pattern \"malformed stored|HTTP distinguishes malformed\" test/decision-inbox.test.ts test/decision-inbox-routes.test.ts. (4) Only respondToDecision release handling reverted: 0/1 pass; real installed file-lock provider removed its owned lock then rejected, masking the committed result. Command: node scripts/with-test-db.ts node --test --test-name-pattern \"cleanup failure\" test/decision-inbox.test.ts. (5) Only listDecisionInbox reverted: 0/1 pass, failed complete read escaped DEPENDENCY_FAILED. Command: node scripts/with-test-db.ts node --test --test-name-pattern \"CLI inbox refusals\" test/decision-inbox.test.ts. All five builds and test processes exited as expected; restored source was rebuilt. No SDK mocks; fixtures use real non-git trackers, installed extensions and PostgreSQL HTTP."
  "2026-10-22T13:55:04.436Z",codex-agent,"Restored-source verification: the existing linked SDK/CLI/HTTP command passed 27/27 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations; pm test --run --progress --only-index 1 --pm-context tracker --override-linked-pm-context passed 1/1 linked command. npm run build and npm run build:test passed; npm run lint passed; unchanged duplication gate is 0 percent with 0 clone pairs; docstring gate documents all 821 declarations in 155 files. Normal pm health --strict-exit passes all 10 checks, with only stale-work advisory. Initial local extension version skew was resolved by the existing CI install-pm-github.sh script using its pinned version; no dependency pins changed. Latest published pm CLI is 2026.10.22; repository SDK remains pinned 2026.10.19 as required. Committed dist rebuilt. Full npm and Bun gates will run in the existing Node 22/26 CI matrix."
